From 220a929218374b7a31c79e0273b8730c49e36baa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Malard <malard@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:01:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [JSON-RPC][VideoLibrary] Apply a TV show's playcount and
 lastplayed to its episodes

VideoLibrary.SetTVShowDetails accepts playcount and lastplayed and copies both into the show's
tag, but UpdateDetailsForTvShow writes only tvshow table columns. A show has no file row of its
own - its playcount is derived from its episodes - so both values were dropped and the method
answered OK.

The values now go to every episode of the show, the way the GUI's mark-watched path resolves a
show to its episodes. The guard is whether the parameter was given, not the value-changed
comparison the sibling setters use: a partly watched show already reads back the derived
playcount 0, so an unwatch request would compare equal and do nothing. An episode already at
the requested playcount is left alone unless a lastplayed is also given, and a playcount-only
change keeps each episode's own lastplayed rather than stamping every one with the time of the
call. Each write announces the episode's update as playing it would.

Fixes #21781

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit b0d8f938fe786564044aa409c802cf541d145655)
